At Mirror App, we value your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information when you use our mobile application. Our primary goal is to provide a useful utility while ensuring your data remains private and secure.
1. Information Collection and Use
We do not collect, store, or share any personal information.
•
Camera Data: The app requires access to your device’s camera to provide the mirror functionality. This data is processed in real-time on your device and is never uploaded to any servers or shared with third parties.
•
Images & Screenshots: If you use the "Capture" or "Freeze" feature, images are saved directly to your device's local gallery. We do not have access to these images, and they are not transmitted off your device.
2. Permissions
To function correctly, the app requests the following permissions:
•
Camera: Necessary to display the live mirror feed.
•
Storage (Media): Necessary to save captured screenshots to your photo gallery.
•
Internet: Used solely for displaying advertisements and basic app performance analytics.
•
Keep Screen On: Used to prevent the screen from dimming while you are using the mirror.
3. Advertising
Our app uses Our Ads Partner (Start.io) to display advertisements. These ads help us keep the app free for everyone.
•
Our advertising partners may use anonymous identifiers (such as the Android Advertising ID) to serve personalized ads based on your interests.
•
You can opt out of interest-based advertising in your Android device settings (Settings > Google > Ads > Opt out of Ads Personalization).
4. No Personal Data Sharing
We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your personal data to outside parties. Since we do not collect personal information (such as names, emails, or phone numbers), there is no data to share.
5. Children’s Privacy
Our app does not collect any information from children. It is a simple utility tool safe for users of all ages.
